<title>USA: SubMicron Systems gets orders for $21 mln.</title>
<headline>SubMicron Systems gets orders for $21 mln.</headline>
<dateline>ALLENTOWN, Pa. 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>SubMicron Systems Corp said on Tuesday that it has received repeat orders in excess of $21 million from two major international customers.</p>
<p>SubMicron, a supplier of wafer processing equipment to the semiconductor industry, said that the contracts include its first production order for its new DIO3 process.</p>
<p>It said its DI03 process eliminates the use of sulfuric acid in photo-resist stripping.</p>
</text>
